# Configuration for deploy/deploy.sh, which ships this checkout to the host
# from your own machine. To use it:
#
#     cp deploy/deploy.env.example deploy/deploy.env && chmod 600 deploy/deploy.env
#
# Then fill in the values below. The 600 is not advice: this file holds
# MAPILLARY_TOKEN, and deploy.sh refuses to run if anything but its owner can
# read it. deploy/deploy.env is gitignored; keep it that way.
#
# The file is SOURCED as shell, so USE SINGLE QUOTES for every value:
# TOKEN='...', not TOKEN="...". Inside double quotes a backtick runs a command,
# a `$NAME` is substituted away if that name happens to be set in your shell
# (and aborts the deploy with `unbound variable` if it is not), and a trailing
# backslash swallows the next line. A Mapillary token is exactly the kind of
# opaque string that can contain one of those by chance, and the deploy would
# then write a silently wrong token into backend/.env on the host and report
# success. Single quotes mean the value is taken literally; the only thing you
# cannot put in them is a single quote.
#
# Quoting a value with a space in it works, and the deploy will then refuse it
# anyway, because rsync's --rsh string is split on whitespace and a space
# cannot be carried through it. The meanings here are
# the same as the repository secrets in docs/DEPLOY.md step 5, with one
# difference and one addition:
#
#   There is no DEPLOY_HOST_KEY. The host key comes from your own
#   ~/.ssh/known_hosts, verified interactively once, which is a better pin than
#   a blob pasted into a settings page. `Host key verification failed` from the
#   deploy means there is no entry yet: ssh to the host by hand once, check the
#   fingerprint, accept it. A host key that CHANGES will stop the deploy, which
#   is the wanted behaviour.
#
#   SSH_KEY is new, because the key is a file on this machine rather than a
#   secret the pipeline writes out.

# The server's own hostname, not a Cloudflare-proxied domain: a proxied domain
# forwards HTTP and drops port 22, so ssh to it can never work.
DEPLOY_HOST=

# The cPanel account the deploy connects as.
DEPLOY_USER=

# The subdomain's document root on the host, absolute, no trailing slash. This
# is PRODUCTION: `deploy/deploy.sh --target /home/USER/tours-staging` overrides
# it for a rehearsal without touching this file.
DEPLOY_PATH=

# Written to backend/.env on the host, and only when that file does not already
# exist -- backend/.env is host-owned state. Rotating the token here does NOT
# update the host; edit backend/.env there.
MAPILLARY_TOKEN=

# Optional. The private half of the deploy key, passphraseless (the deploy sets
# BatchMode=yes, so nothing can answer a prompt). Default:
# $HOME/.ssh/clio_deploy, which is where docs/DEPLOY.md's `ssh-keygen` puts it.
#SSH_KEY=

# Optional. Default 22.
#DEPLOY_PORT=
